why: the operator asked whether the arc covers what Spring Boot,
  Guice, Dagger, ZLayer and distage offer. The answer is mostly yes,
  partly by-other-means, and partly NO — and a reader deciding
  whether to adopt this deserves that list rather than a claim.

what: a capability-by-capability table in docs/di.md: what each
  feature is for, how it is spelled here, and where we have nothing.
  Every OUR-side cell must be true of the code today — including the
  four gaps I know of (no set-binding, no memoisation of a module
  used twice, no AOP, no events) and the deliberate absences with
  their reasons.

